      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s first post office opened July 3, 1837, and by the 1840s it was one of South Georgia’s most prosperous towns.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walthourville%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1857 the Savannah, Albany & Gulf Railroad reached Walthourville, linking it to Savannah and Bainbridge.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walthourville%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Walthourville Presbyterian Church, built in 1820, later earned a spot on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
